{"parentUuid":"7822b137-35de-47d9-bd6c-1f6f66abafb8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdbWYfc1sWrgKdMDWRVGL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both landed. Full suite: **172 files / 1661 tests pass**, typecheck + selector lint clean.\n\n**1. Scheduler now shows the originating Epic — from one source**\n\nThe root problem was that three fields could each claim to be \"the Epic\", and in your live `queue.json` they already disagree (`sourcePromptId: psess-ms9x7241-9` vs `sourceTabId: epic-scheduler-integration-audit-…`). Worse, only the Queue read one of them (`sourceTabId` alone), so the same PRD showed a different Epic — or none — depending on the tab.\n\n- **Backend**: `parsePrd` now emits `epicId` derived from the PRD's *directory* (`scheduler/epics/<id>/prds/`) — fact on disk, 1:1 by design — separate from the intent-carrying `sourcePromptId`. Threaded into queue rows (`scheduler.cjs`, both the new-entry and reconcile paths) and `schedule:list-prds`. Unlike `sourcePromptId`, `epicId` is refreshed from disk every reconcile, so moving a PRD between Epic dirs re-points its row. `originSessionId` now resolves off it too.\n- **`lib/epicProvenance.ts`**: one resolver, `epicId → sourcePromptId → sourceTabId`, where a candidate that *resolves* beats one that doesn't — so the stale-id rows above land on the real Epic instead of rendering a bare id.\n- **`EpicTag`** in `sched-primitives.tsx`, wired into **Queue rows, PRD cards, and History rows** (plus `epic` detail lines), clickable through to the Epic. The PRDs view was dropping `sourcePromptId` in a local interface — that's why it showed nothing.\n- Scheduler now hydrates prompt-sessions (active + archived) for its scoped project, so booting straight into it shows Epic names rather than ids.\n\nExisting queue rows gain `epicId` on the next reconcile tick; until then the fallback resolves them.\n\n**2. New Epic auto-sends its objective**\n\n`lib/epicI