{"parentUuid":"faee12cd-dd0d-45ec-a70c-971ee346ea76","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdbY87trRSmCGLJP7TYHi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is green: **176 test files / 1674 tests pass**, `lint:selectors` OK, typecheck clean except one pre-existing issue noted below.\n\n**1. Single-writer law** — `src/main/lib/opsOwnership.cjs`\n\nEach `session-manager-operations/<namespace>/` has exactly one owning writer; everyone reads freely. `prompt-sessions→epics`, `scheduler→scheduler`, `project-brief→project-home`, `feedback→feedback`, `browser→browser`. **Fail-closed**: an undeclared writer, or a namespace with no declared owner, throws.\n\nEnforcing only in `config.cjs` would have been a fake law — `epicMint` and `queueStore` write with raw `fs` and would have sailed straight through. All three call the gate. Renderer callers declare through IPC (`config.writeJson(path, data, 'epics')`).\n\nOne narrow, path-scoped **delegation** exists: the scheduler writing `prompt-sessions/active-index.json` (it appends Epic events with no renderer attached). It's declared in one table with its reason rather than left as an undocumented cross-write. The law immediately caught two real call sites in `prdCreate`'s tests.\n\n**2. Epic first-prompt + immutable goal** — title/objective compose through `lib/epicIntake.ts` and are sent at creation. `goalText` is written once and nothing mutates it, as you asked.\n\n**3. Scheduler shows its Epic** — `epicId` (derived from the PRD's directory, the authoritative 1:1 source) now flows through parser → queue rows → `list-prds`, with one shared resolver (`lib/epicProvenance.ts`) behind an `EpicTag` on Queue, PRDs, and History. Your live `queue.json` had rows where `sourcePromptId` and `sourceTabId` disagreed; the resolver prefers a candidate that actually resolves.\n\n**4. Feedback → proposed Epics.** `status: 'proposed'` + `EpicApprovalBar` (Approve & start / Discard) + `scripts/propose-epic.cjs`. The RCA hook now files a proposal instead of markdown — a re-trigger *enriches the pending proposal in place* (a proposal hasn't started, so its opening prompt is still legitimately mutable; an active Epic's never is). Deleted: `/process-feedback`, `/my-feedback` (405 lines → one ~60-line `/propose-epic`), the 5-minute scheduler feedback sweep, and the RCA file-inbox dedupe logic. Updated the 26 references across the other skills. Also deleted `/optimize-kpi` and removed `project-status`'s dependence on it and on the `-local` this project doesn't have.\n\n**5. PRD 865 (paste image)** — taken over and fixed. Two real defects: `onPaste` was bound only to the attachment *tray*, so pasting while typing in the textarea did nothing despite the placeholder advertising ⌘V; and `NewEpicCard` inlined `item.path`, which for a pasted image is the bare filename `pasted-image.png` — a reference to a file that never existed. Shared `attachPastedFiles` + `resolveAttachmentPaths` now cover both composers. Regression tests added; the PRD source is archived to `prds-archived/` so the scheduler won't redo it.\n\nTwo things worth your attention:\n\n- **`EpicDetail.tsx` has in-flight edits that aren't mine** — it calls a `captureTerminalHandoffTurns` that doesn't exist yet, and it's the *only* typecheck failure. I left it alone rather than guessing at someone else's half-finished work.\n- I corrected myself mid-way: I said the plugin was outside this repo. It's at `plugins/session-manager-dev/`, and it's registered as a `directory` marketplace pointing at this repo — so the skill edits above are real and in-tree."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":312270,"output_tokens":1315,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250,"ephemeral_5m_input_